/packages/**/*.d.ts.map
/packages/**/*.d.ts

# **Hand-written ambient declarations, not build output.** Every package builds
# with `outDir: '.'`, so generated `.d.ts` land beside the entrypoints and never
# under `src/` — but the blanket rule above swallowed the authored ones too, and
# `packages/drag2/src/globals.d.ts` is the whole `__DEV__` declaration: without
# it a fresh clone cannot typecheck that package at all.
#
# ~~`!/packages/*/src`~~ was the intended fix and is a **no-op**: nothing above
# excludes the `src` directory itself, and git cannot re-include a file by
# re-including a directory that was never excluded. The negation has to name the
# files, which is the form the `bench` exceptions below already use.
#
# Deliberately `.d.ts` only. `.js`, `.js.map` and `.d.ts.map` under `src/` stay
# ignored, so this admits authored declarations and no emitted artifact.
!/packages/*/src/**/*.d.ts

# **Hand-written measurement fixtures, not build output** (P18A-16). The M-3
# size baselines are authored `.js`/`.d.ts` by necessity — baseline A assembles
# a slot record by hand and baseline B is a different package — so the blanket
# rules above made one of D-77's own measurements, and the test that keeps the
# baseline honest against `assemble()`, unreproducible from a clean clone.
!/packages/*/bench/**/*.js
!/packages/*/bench/**/*.d.ts

